      "heading_context": "## Decision Cheat Sheet",
      "headers": [
        "Question",
        "Answer"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "What is the Talmud?",
          "Mishnah (oral law codified ~200 CE) + Gemara (rabbinic commentary) = Talmud. The Babylonian Talmud (~500 CE) is authoritative."
        ],
        [
          "Why did Judaism survive the Temple's destruction?",
          "Rabbinic revolution: replaced Temple/sacrifice with synagogue/study/prayer. Portable religion."
        ],
        [
          "What was decided at Nicaea?",
          "Homoousios: Jesus is of same substance as the Father. Arianism (Jesus is lesser, created) condemned."
        ],
        [
          "What is the Chalcedonian formula?",
          "Jesus has two natures (divine + human) in one person, without confusion or separation. ~451 CE."
        ],
        [
          "Why Sunni vs. Shia?",
          "Succession dispute after Muhammad's death (632 CE). Sunni: elected Caliph. Shia: Ali (Muhammad's cousin/son-in-law) as rightful Imam. Karbala (680 CE) sealed the split."
        ],
        [
          "What is sharia?",
          "Islamic law derived from Quran, Sunna (hadith), ijma (consensus), and qiyas (analogy). Not a single code — a tradition of legal reasoning."
        ],
        [
          "What is the difference between Quran and hadith?",
          "Quran = God's direct speech. Hadith = reports of Muhammad's words/actions. Different authority, different textual status."
        ]
      ]
    }
